---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects" description="Compass and the engineering work behind the writing: a local companion for selected project context and a limited metadata audit trail.">
  <div class="shell page-width">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">The work behind the writing</p>
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p>Code and experiments that give these essays something concrete to talk about.</p>
    </header>
    {projects.map((project) => <article class="project-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
      <h2>{project.title}</h2>
      <p class="project-description">{project.description}</p>
      <p>The coding tool’s native harness still owns execution, approvals, and its security boundaries. This companion uses the integration points the tool exposes.</p>
      <div class="project-capabilities">
        <div><h3>Shared core</h3><p>Metadata contracts, redaction, a local ledger, and a dashboard.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Separate adapters</h3><p>Automatic grounding, audit collection, credential-pattern observations, and the dashboard support Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="project-limit">The companion supplies project context and observes activity. Execution, approvals, and context history remain with the native coding tool; the credential scanner does not block agent actions.</p>
      <p class="project-stack">{project.language}</p>
      <div class="project-links">
        <a class="text-link" href={project.repository}>View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={project.article}>Read the first essay <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>)}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
